== (6) Proposition 9.3(ii): the conclusion needs gamma <= 1/2 ==
   The protocol that asks nothing (n = 0) and answers every call with a fair coin has failure probability
   Pr[maj != sigma_z] = 1/2 for odd L, for every sigma.  With gamma = 1/2 the stated bound is n >= 0: true.
   With gamma = 0.9 the stated bound reads n >= K (1 - 1.8)^2/(8 theta'^2) = 0.08 K/theta'^2 > 0, which this
   protocol violates (failure 1/2 <= 0.9, n = 0).  So (ii) must assume gamma <= 1/2.

